  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material implying shared responsibility or complicity",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the textual material 'in 2016 they proved it', which uses the pronoun 'they' to refer to the American voters. This creates a semiotic projection where the viewer is positioned as part of the group 'they'—the voters who allegedly 'proved' Trump's statement by electing him. This projection invites the user to identify with the voters and internalize the meme's narrative that their collective action validated a derogatory claim about themselves, fostering a sense of shared identity or complicity in the meme's divisive message.",
